# The SMK-37 build: all 37 keys are the scale, the pads are the 16 white keys (the scale with low notes on the
# bottom row; the effects grid, PERFORM and the Pattern page in reading order), their lights, the fader banks, the
# wheels, < and >, the picker (KNOB BANK)
listen
wait 3000
expect playing 1
expect pool 0x6AD
# F Dorian. C3 (keybed key 0) is C, the fifth: out; C6 (key 36) puts it back
kbkey 0
expect pool 0x62D
kbkey 36
expect pool 0x6AD
# the middle keys as on the FM-1: F#3 in and out
tapkey b0
expect pool 0x6AF
tapkey b0
expect pool 0x6AD
# the pads: the white keys F3..G5, the bottom row first. Pad 8 is F3, the root: it stays; pad 9 is G3
expect padlayout 0
pad 8
wait 200
said THE ROOT STAYS
pad 9
expect pool 0x6A9
pad 9
expect pool 0x6AD
# the top row from G4: pad 0 is G4, the same note
pad 0
expect pool 0x6A9
pad 0
expect pool 0x6AD
# their lights: the root a stronger blue, a note out of the scale (A3, pad 10) dark orange
wait 1000
pads
expect padg8 >150
expect padr10 >90
expect padb10 <20
# the effects grid: REC held, the pads in reading order (pad 4 is the fifth effect, Low-pass)
press REC
wait 400
said EFFECTS GRID
expect padlayout 1
expect padg0 >80
expect padg1 <90
pad 4 down
wait 300
said Low-pass
pads
expect padg4 >200
release REC
wait 300
pad 4 up
wait 800
expect frozen 0
expect padlayout 0
# PERFORM (SEL): pads 1-5 the mutes, 6-10 the moves held (the top row first)
tap SEL
wait 200
said PERFORM ON
expect padlayout 1
pad 3
wait 200
said KICK OFF
pad 3
wait 200
said KICK ON
pad 5 down
wait 200
said THROW
expect padr5 >200
pad 5 up
wait 200
expect padr5 <90
tap SEL
wait 200
said PERFORM OFF
expect padlayout 0
# the Pattern page: the pads its sixteen steps in reading order; a black key held with a pad: an accent
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
wait 400
expect view 16
expect padlayout 1
pad 3
wait 200
said Step 4 on
expect par105 1
expect padb3 >150
key b0 down
pad 2
key b0 up
wait 200
said Step 3 accented
expect par94 4
tap SEQ
wait 300
expect view 4
expect padlayout 0
# the Chords page: the pads and the outer keys set the slot's root (D3, keybed key 2: D)
tap EDIT
wait 400
expect view 15
kbkey 2
wait 200
expect par64 2
pad 9
wait 200
expect par64 7
tap EDIT
wait 300
expect view 4
# the faders: bank B, the space; a fader takes over once it moves
sbtn FADER_BANK
expect fbank 1
expect fcard 1
expect smkleds 2
fader 0 127
expect par8 100
fader 2 0
expect par11 0
shot faders.png
wait 2000
expect fcard 0
# bank C: the shape, Cutoff first (the first reading after a bank change only sets where the fader is)
sbtn FADER_BANK
expect fbank 2
fader 0 0
expect par12 0
fader 0 64
expect par12 50
# back to A, the levels
sbtn FADER_BANK
expect fbank 0
expect smkleds 0
fader 0 0
expect par0 0
fader 0 64
expect par0 50
# the wheels: the tape and the filter, never saved
wheel pitch 127
wheel mod 127
wait 200
expect warp 127
expect par12 50
wheel pitch 0
wheel mod 0
wait 200
expect warp 0
# < > the pages, as SELECT
tap HOME
sbtn RIGHT
expect view 1
sbtn RIGHT
expect view 2
sbtn LEFT
sbtn LEFT
sbtn LEFT
expect view 0
# the picker (KNOB BANK): the top row the pieces, the bottom row the modes; the pads pick, not play
sbtn KNOB_BANK
expect picker 1
expect smkleds 1
expect padlayout 2
wait 200
shot picker.png
pads
# the picker's states: the other pieces on (light blue), the piece playing active (bright)
expect padb2 >150
expect padr2 <90
expect padr0 >150
pad 2
wait 200
expect piece 2
expect padr2 >150
expect padr0 <90
pad 13
wait 200
expect par20 5
expect pool 0x5AD
sbtn KNOB_BANK
expect picker 0
expect padlayout 0
expect smkleds 0
shot main.png
